 ## Overview
-A projection-based ray-casting algorithm for curvilinear grids (hexahedra) that finds the first face by scan-converting boundary faces, then projects all faces to find exit points [S1, unofficial]. It is a very fast ray-casting technique exploiting the special topology of curvilinear grids [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent, [Hexahedron Projection for Curvilinear Grids](1111-hexahedron-projection-for-curvilinear-grids.md), by using a projection-based traversal strategy rather than hardware rasterization of triangle fans/strips, and from its sibling [Depthless Cell Face Projection](6692-depthless-cell-face-projection.md) by explicitly handling the non-planar geometry of curvilinear hexahedra via on-the-fly triangulation and ray-crossing tests.
