 ## How it works
-**Inputs:**
-- Curvilinear grid data (hexahedral cells with non-planar faces).
-- Viewpoint and projection parameters.
-- Scalar field values associated with grid nodes.
-
-**Outputs:**
-- Rendered image with accumulated color and opacity.
-
-**Data Structures:**
-- Hexahedron representation: 8 vertices per cell, each with 3D coordinates $(x, y, z)$.
-- Face representation: Each hexahedron has 6 faces. Each face is decomposed into 2 triangles, resulting in 12 triangles per hexahedron.
-- Image plane: 2D coordinate system for projection.
