 5. **Find Exit Face:**
-   - **Original Approach:** Test the remaining eleven triangles sequentially until an intersected triangle (exit face) is found [S1, unofficial]. One triangle is already known as the entry face.
-   - **Follow-up Approach:** Group the remaining eleven triangles and project them onto the image plane [S1, unofficial]. Find the exiting triangle using a ray-crossing technique [Haines94]. A point $P$ is inside a 2D polygon if a horizontal ray from $P$ to the right crosses polygon edges an odd number of times [S1, unofficial]. By checking how many times this horizontal ray crosses the edges of tested triangles, the exiting triangle, and hence the exiting face, can be determined [S1, unofficial].
